Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; Stained Glass OS: a Control Panel item (.cpl) opens with "open" too, as
; with its own verb cplopen. Run's "sysdm.cpl" and `start sysdm.cpl` ask for
; "open" by name, and a .cpl has only cplopen: "There is no program
; configured to open this type of file" (QA 2026-10-02).

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\Software\Classes\cplfile\shell\open]
@="Open with Control Panel"

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\Software\Classes\cplfile\shell\open\command]
@="rundll32.exe shell32.dll,Control_RunDLL \"%1\",%*"
